en.fuller:
ἵνα,
__I. adverb (poët., Hom., al.),
__1. of place, where, whither.
__2. of circumstance, when.
__II. Conjunction,
__1. prop., final, denoting purpose or end (cl.), that, in order that, usually the first word in the clause, but sometimes (cl. also) preceded by an emphatic word (Act.19:4, Rom.11:31 (?), Gal.2:10, al.);
__(a) with optative (so in cl. after historic tenses): after a pres., Eph.1:17 (but WH, mg., subjc.; see Burton, §225, Rem., 2);
__(b) with subjc.: after a pres., Mrk.4:21, Luk.6:34, Jhn.3:15, Act.2:25, Rom.1:11, al.; after a pf., Mat.1:22, Jhn.5:23 1Co.9:22, al.; after an imperat. (present or aor.), Mat.7:1, Mrk.11:25, Jhn.10:38, 1Co.7:5, al.; after a delib. subjc., Mrk.1:38, al.; after a fut., Luk.16:4, Jhn.14:3, 1Co.15:28, al.; after historic tenses (where optative in cl.; WM, 359f.; M, Pr., 196f.), Mrk.6:41 (impf.), Jhn.4:8 (plpf.), Mrk.3:14 (aor.), al.;
__(with) in late writers (M, Pr., 35; Burton, §§198, 199), with indic., fut: Luk.20:10, 1Pe.3:1, al.;
__(d) as often in eccl. writers (Thayer, see word), with indic. pres.: 1Co.4:6, Gal.4:17, al. (?; but V. Burton, §198, Rem.);
__(e) εἰς (διὰ) τοῦτο, ἵνα: Jhn.18:37, 1Ti.1:16, al.; τούτου χάριν, Tit.1:5;
__(f) elliptical constructions: omission of the principal verb, Jhn.1:8, 2Th.3:9, 1Jn.2:19, al.; of the final verb, Rom.4:16, 2Co.8:13, al.
__2. In late writers, definitive, = inf. (WM, 420; Bl, §69, 1), that;
__(a) after verbs of wishing, caring, striving, etc.: θέλω, Mat.7:12, al.; ζητῶ, 1Co.4:2 14:12; ζηλόω, 1Co.14:1, al.;
__(b) after verbs of saying, asking, exhorting: εἰπεῖν, Mat.4:3, al.; ἐρωτῶ, Mrk.7:26, al.; παρακαλῶ, Mat.14:36, 1Co.1:10, al., etc.;
__(with) after words expressing expediency, etc.: συμφέρει, Mat.18:6, Jhn.11:50, al.; ἱκανός, Mat.8:8, Luk.7:6; χρείαν ἔχω, Jhn.2:25, al, etc.;
__(d) after substantives, adding further definition: ὥρα, Jhn.12:23 13:1; χρόνος, Rev.2:21; συνήθεια, Jhn.18:39; μισθός, 1Co.9:18.
__3. In late writers, ecbatic, denoting the result, = ὥστε, that, so that (M, Pr., 206ff.; WM, 572; Bl., §69, 3; Burton, §223): Rom.11:11, 1Co.7:29, 1Th.5:4, al. (but see Thayer, see word); so with the formula referring to the fulfilment of prophecy, ἵνα πληρωθῇ, Mat.1:22 2:14, Jhn.13:18, al.
(AS)

es.fuller:
ἵνα,
I. adverb (poët., Hom., etc.),
1. of place, where, whither.
2. of circumstance, when.
II. Conjunction,
1. prop., final, denoting purpose or end (clás.), that, in order that, usually the first word in the clause, but sometimes (clás. also) preceded by an emphatic word (Hch.19:4, Ro.11:31 (?), Gá.2:10, etc.);
(a) con opt. (so en clás. after historic tenses): after a pres., Ef.1:17 (but WH, mg., subjc.; see Burton, §225, Rem., 2);
(b) con subj..: after a pres., Mc.4:21, Lc.6:34, Jn.3:15, Hch.2:25, Ro.1:11, etc.; after a pf., Mt.1:22, Jn.5:23 1Co.9:22, etc.; after an imperat. (present or aor.), Mt.7:1, Mc.11:25, Jn.10:38, 1Co.7:5, etc.; after a delib. subjc., Mc.1:38, etc.; after a fut., Lc.16:4, Jn.14:3, 1Co.15:28, etc.; after historic tenses (where optative en clás.; WM, 359f.; M, Pr., 196f.), Mc.6:41 (impf.), Jn.4:8 (plpf.), Mc.3:14 (aor.), etc.;
(with) in late writers (M, Pr., 35; Burton, §§198, 199), con indic., fut: Lc.20:10, 1P.3:1, etc.;
(d) as often in eccl. writers (Thayer, véase), con indic. pres.: 1Co.4:6, Gá.4:17, etc. (?; but V. Burton, §198, Rem.);
(e) εἰς (διὰ) τοῦτο, ἵνα: Jn.18:37, 1Ti.1:16, etc.; τούτου χάριν, Tit.1:5;
(f) elliptical constructions: omission of the principal verb, Jn.1:8, 2Ts.3:9, 1Jn.2:19, etc.; of the final verb, Ro.4:16, 2Co.8:13, etc.
2. In late writers, definitive, = inf. (WM, 420; Bl, §69, 1), that;
(a) after verbs of wishing, caring, striving, etc.: θέλω, Mt.7:12, etc.; ζητῶ, 1Co.4:2 14:12; ζηλόω, 1Co.14:1, etc.;
(b) after verbs of saying, asking, exhorting: εἰπεῖν, Mt.4:3, etc.; ἐρωτῶ, Mc.7:26, etc.; παρακαλῶ, Mt.14:36, 1Co.1:10, etc., etc.;
(with) after words expressing expediency, etc.: συμφέρει, Mt.18:6, Jn.11:50, etc.; ἱκανός, Mt.8:8, Lc.7:6; χρείαν ἔχω, Jn.2:25, al, etc.;
(d) after substantives, adding further definition: ὥρα, Jn.12:23 13:1; χρόνος, Ap.2:21; συνήθεια, Jn.18:39; μισθός, 1Co.9:18.
3. In late writers, ecbatic, denoting the result, = ὥστε, that, so that (M, Pr., 206ff.; WM, 572; Bl., §69, 3; Burton, §223): Ro.11:11, 1Co.7:29, 1Ts.5:4, etc. (but véase Thayer, véase); so with the formula referring to the fulfilment of prophecy, ἵνα πληρωθῇ, Mt.1:22 2:14, Jn.13:18, etc.
(AS)

he.fuller:
ἵνα,
I. adverb (poët., Hom., ועוד),
1. of place, where, whither.
2. of circumstance, when.
II. Conjunction,
1. בעיקרו, final, denoting purpose or end (קלאסית), that, in order that, usually the first word in the clause, but sometimes (קלאסית also) preceded by an emphatic word (מע״ש.19:4, רומים.11:31 (?), גל.2:10, ועוד);
(a) עם אופטי (so בקלאסית after historic tenses): after a pres., אפ.1:17 (but WH, mg., subjc.; see Burton, §225, Rem., 2);
(b) עם משאלה.: after a pres., מרקוס.4:21, לוקס.6:34, יוחנן.3:15, מע״ש.2:25, רומים.1:11, ועוד; after a pf., מתי.1:22, יוחנן.5:23 1קור.9:22, ועוד; after an imperat. (present or עבר), מתי.7:1, מרקוס.11:25, יוחנן.10:38, 1קור.7:5, ועוד; after a delib. subjc., מרקוס.1:38, ועוד; after a fut., לוקס.16:4, יוחנן.14:3, 1קור.15:28, ועוד; after historic tenses (where optative בקלאסית; WM, 359f.; M, Pr., 196f.), מרקוס.6:41 (impf.), יוחנן.4:8 (plpf.), מרקוס.3:14 (עבר), ועוד;
(with) in late writers (M, Pr., 35; Burton, §§198, 199), עם מציאות, fut: לוקס.20:10, 1פ.3:1, ועוד;
(d) as often in eccl. writers (Thayer, ר׳ ערך), עם מציאות pres.: 1קור.4:6, גל.4:17, ועוד (?; but V. Burton, §198, Rem.);
(e) εἰς (διὰ) τοῦτο, ἵνα: יוחנן.18:37, 1טי.1:16, ועוד; τούτου χάριν, טיט.1:5;
(f) elliptical constructions: omission of the principal verb, יוחנן.1:8, 2תס.3:9, 1יוח.2:19, ועוד; of the final verb, רומים.4:16, 2קור.8:13, ועוד
2. In late writers, definitive, = מקור (WM, 420; Bl, §69, 1), that;
(a) after verbs of wishing, caring, striving, ועוד: θέλω, מתי.7:12, ועוד; ζητῶ, 1קור.4:2 14:12; ζηλόω, 1קור.14:1, ועוד;
(b) after verbs of saying, asking, exhorting: εἰπεῖν, מתי.4:3, ועוד; ἐρωτῶ, מרקוס.7:26, ועוד; παρακαλῶ, מתי.14:36, 1קור.1:10, ועוד, ועוד;
(with) after words expressing expediency, ועוד: συμφέρει, מתי.18:6, יוחנן.11:50, ועוד; ἱκανός, מתי.8:8, לוקס.7:6; χρείαν ἔχω, יוחנן.2:25, al, ועוד;
(d) after substantives, adding further definition: ὥρα, יוחנן.12:23 13:1; χρόνος, התג.2:21; συνήθεια, יוחנן.18:39; μισθός, 1קור.9:18.
3. In late writers, ecbatic, denoting the result, = ὥστε, that, so that (M, Pr., 206ff.; WM, 572; Bl., §69, 3; Burton, §223): רומים.11:11, 1קור.7:29, 1תס.5:4, ועוד (but ר׳ Thayer, ר׳ ערך); so with the formula referring to the fulfilment of prophecy, ἵνα πληρωθῇ, מתי.1:22 2:14, יוחנן.13:18, ועוד
(AS)

